    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§203 & 204, Ag & Mkts L",
    "lawSection": "Agriculture and Markets Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S5751\n\nSPONSOR: HINCHEY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the agriculture and markets law, in relation to the\nmanufacturing, sale, branding and labeling of beech sugar and beech\nsyrup\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this legislation is add the products of beech syrup and\nbeech sugar into the current law in an effort to provide protection to\nconsumers who purchase these products and to also maintain the integrity\nof the products for the farmers who produce these syrups and blends.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Section 203 of the Agriculture and Markets Law would be\namended to prohibit the manufacture for sale or sale of beech syrup that\nwas not made from pure beech sap or syrup.\n\nSection 2: Section 204 of the Agriculture and Markets Law would be\namended to prohibit the manufacture for sale or sale of a mixture of\nbeech sugar or syrup with other sugars or syrups or substances without\nbranding or labeling the product with all the ingredients.\n\nSection 3: Sets forth the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation would add beech syrup and beech sugar into the list of\nsyrups that have been defined in law. The clear definition of these\nproducts assists consumers and provides Truth in Labeling, so consumers\nare confident in their purchases. It also protects producers of pure\nsyrup and sugar from unfair competition with diluted products that may\nappear to be pure.  New York State is the second largest producer of\nmaple syrup in the United States and the maple industry is highly active\nin many portions of the state with sugar shacks and Maple Weekend activ-\nities.  Our Maple farmers continue to expand the use of their products\nand create new varieties of syrup.\n\nThis legislation will expand the current \"Truth in Labeling\" provisions\nin current law covering maple, birch and walnut syrup to included beech\nsyrup and beech sugar in the list of syrups provided protections.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is new legislation.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nThis legislation will have no fiscal implications for the State or local\ngovernments.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis bill would take effect immediately.\n",
